{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-5692005ebe1ad2bf6fab","statement":"Suppose we have $(\\bfC_i, \\verti_i, \\horiz_i),\\ i=1,2$, and a finite limit preserving fully faithful embedding $\\bfC_1\\subset \\bfC_2$ which induces fully faithful embeddings $(\\bfC_1)_{\\verti_1}\\subset (\\bfC_2)_{\\verti_2}, (\\bfC_1)_{\\horiz_1}\\subset (\\bfC_2)_{\\horiz_2}$. Suppose Assumption <<ref:prop-sheaf-theory-right-Kan-extension-1>> in <<ref:prop-sheaf-theory-right-Kan-extension>> holds, and suppose $\\verti_1$ is strongly stable. Let $\\verti_{2,r}\\subset \\verti_2$ be the subset of morphisms are that representable in $\\verti_1$. Let\n\n\\begin{equation}\n\\der_1: \\corr(\\bfC_1)_{\\verti_1;\\horiz_1}\\to \\lincat_\\La\n\\end{equation}\n\nbe a sheaf theory.\n\nSuppose that there is a strongly stable class $\\mathrm{S}_1\\subset\\verti_1\\cap \\horiz_1$, satisfying the following conditions.\nLet $\\mathrm{S}_2\\subset \\verti_2\\cap \\horiz_2$ be the subset of morphisms that are representable in $\\mathrm{S}_1$. For every $X\\in \\bfC_2$, write $\\mS_X:=(\\bfC_1)_{\\mathrm{S}_1}\\times_{(\\bfC_2)_{\\mathrm{S}_2}}((\\bfC_2)_{\\mathrm{S}_2})_{/X}$. Then\n\n- For every $(f: X\\to Y)\\in\\bfC_{\\verti_2}$ and $(g: X'\\to X)\\in \\mS_X$, the composition $(f\\circ g: X'\\to Y)\\in \\bfC_{\\verti_{2,r}}$, and for every $(f: X\\to Y)\\in\\bfC_{\\verti_{2,r}}$ and $(g: X'\\to X)\\in \\mS_X$, the composition $f\\circ g: X'\\to Y$ can be factorized as $X'\\to Y'\\to Y$ with $(Y'\\to Y)\\in \\mS_Y$.\n\n- The inclusion $\\mS_X\\to (\\bfC_1)_{\\horiz_1}\\times_{(\\bfC_2)_{\\horiz_2}}((\\bfC_2)_{\\horiz_2})_{/X}$ is cofinal.\n\n- The restriction $\\der_1|_{\\corr((\\bfC_1)_{\\mathrm{S}_1})}$ is isomorphic to sheaf theory from $\\der_1|_{\\corr(\\bfC_1)_{\\isom;\\mathrm{S}_1}}$ by applying <<ref:prop-sheaf-theory-for-adjoint-factorization>> to $\\mathrm{E}=\\mathrm{S}_1$.\n\nThen there is an extension of sheaf theory\n\n\\[\n\\der_2: \\corr(\\bfC_2)_{\\verti_2;\\horiz_2}\\to \\lincat_\\La\n\\]\n\nof <<ref:eq-sheaf-theory-to-be-extended>>\nalong the (non-full) embedding $ \\corr(\\bfC_1)_{\\verti_1;\\all}\\to  \\corr(\\bfC_2)_{\\verti_2;\\all}$, such that\n\n[(a)]\n\n- the restriction $\\der_2|_{\\corr(\\bfC_1)_{\\verti_1, \\horiz_1}}=\\der_1$;\n\n- $\\der|_{((\\bfC_2)_{\\horiz_2})^{\\op}}$ is isomorphic to the right Kan extension of $\\der|_{((\\bfC_1)_{\\horiz_1})^{\\op}}$ along $(\\bfC_1)_{\\horiz_1}\\subset (\\bfC_2)_{\\horiz_2}$.","source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"7fcf9d1593534e0da3bf532a118dd5123246a274aa1918c6481484dabb58f400","kind":"corollary","label":"Corollary 592","ref_key":"prop-sheaf-theory-non-full-right-Kan-extension","name":"","order":839,"deps":[{"ref":"eq-sheaf-theory-to-be-extended","card_id":"ma-c-6c012d52c18008bea9f0","label":"Equation eq-sheaf-theory-to-be-extended","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"prop-sheaf-theory-for-adjoint-factorization","card_id":"ma-c-b7e1c81c298a69532584","label":"Theorem 581","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"prop-sheaf-theory-right-Kan-extension","card_id":"ma-c-6c3ac954765b3ab09259","label":"Proposition 584","resolved":true,"target":"card"},{"ref":"prop-sheaf-theory-right-Kan-extension-1","card_id":null,"label":null,"resolved":false,"target":"statement"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"1b700e8c4a2fc6f0c0f522039f223820ba6737a9a0ac91aea37c58ba7a3389c2","line":16212,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-28T11:10:54+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":2215,"math_hints":232}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","title":"Tame categorical local Langlands correspondence","abstract":"In one of our previous articles, we outlined the formulation of a version of the categorical arithmetic local Langlands c